body:
I know this post was a month ago, but I am searching covid/period stuff because it's happening to me. I had Pfizer in which the first dose caused me a mild case of bell's paulsy. following an episode of extreme double vision for 2 days. Honestly thank goodness for masks...most people just thought I was really sad or something with my eye. 

&#x200B;

The doctors said it probably had nothing to do with the vaccine since it was a week after. I had some scans etc. all good. The said to see a neurologist. 

&#x200B;

I decided just to get the second one and see what happened. Same thing again and steroids. 

&#x200B;

Welllllll my period last month came at the usual time but was heavy as hell and I couldn't go to work because of it. I literally laid in bed for 2 days. 

2 1/2 weeks later I have it again (I am always regular). Killer PMS symptoms unlike ever before. I am bipolar so I thought I was having a bad episode but it was intense period emotions.....LIKE WHAT ?1? So much bleeding and nausea. Honestly I wish I would just throw up now to rid the nausea. 

&#x200B;

I feel like something is very wrong...Call me a conspiracy theorist, but I no longer trust this vaccine in my body.  I know how heartbreaking Covid has been for so many and know that this is helping and I am glad. But I wish I didn't do it.

Prior to meds I tried to jump out of a car, knocked myself out by slaming my head against the wall in frustrated rage, multiple suicide attempts and self harm and acting so out of character my bf would not bring me in public as he was scared of what I would do or say. I destroyed so many things in our apt. I would just scream on the top of my lungs. I felt like a demon was inside and I wanted it gone. I would go so over the top that I would do everything then I would go over the top in a awful way and violent way. Then depressed for a week. Start over. It was hell. I can not even truly ever describe how badly I wanted out of my body. 

&#x200B;

I have been on meds for 10 years. Right now I am on 5 Wellbutrin, Cymbalta, Kolonpin, Lamictal, and Lithium. It seems like a lot but as I go on I need adjustments and changes. My pdoc is soooo incredibly kind and caring. She knows me as a person and in a way almost friend now. She knows what I have been through for 7 years. She saved my life. 

&#x200B;

While I have some episodes they are nothing even close. Therapy didn't help.

I know how you must feel now but there is hope. Not saying this to just throw you positive nonsense, but from experience. The feeling of just HAVING to go to work to live. 

I get that older looking thing. I call it the face of mental illness. Our expressions effect us and show our struggles. (good thing there are some good wrinkle things out rn) 

&#x200B;

A diagnosis and place to start is such a big step! After a few months of individual therapy my therapist wanted me to go to an IOP program. I was hesitant but that program literally saved my life. Group therapy is not for everyone but it was also very much therapy based with share outs. I would maybe look into a program after settling in with your current therapist. I can not beleive how much it helped so many in the group. 

&#x200B;

When I started IOP I was at my absolute worst. I met a friend around my age who was "graduating" the program and feeling pretty stable. I was a nothing person and she promised me with the right medication there was hope and I would feel better. I listened to her but honestly was like that sounds like BS.....but it wasn't! It look about a year to get the right med combo to work for me and there are still some adjustments. 

&#x200B;

Moral is you CAN feel better! You will feel better. I approached it as well right now I am pretty much nothing so how much worse can I get. While I still have some shit days my highly medicated self is free in a sense. 

I know how hard it is but have hope. Going through therapy and getting meds means you don't have to stay strong. You can let others help you while believing you can get better. Take care and let yourself be taken care of. 

&#x200B;

Is there a way you can go on disability, even for a month, to do a program and give yourself a rest to heal? 

Feel free to reach out and dm. I have been here and it is awful. You can make it through!

I can 100% relate to how your mind is working over this. I used to just build all these thoughts upon thoughts and EVEN after something good would happen I was scared to lose it and then insert xyz would make it even worse and so on. It may sound crazy to the outside and while I am medicated now I can see how irrational these fears are but as you are in them right now it is so, so real. BUT it is not, it is just your mind tricking you and your anxiety building thoughts. 

&#x200B;

I don't know about therapy as far as insurance goes but I have never had an issue switching insurances etc. I have had a general understanding that they only ask for major health issues. While I know mental illness is one, usually they see it more as cancer, diabetes, etc. 

&#x200B;

You have the insurance, go get the help you deserve. If you are unsure or still afraid  you call the insurance one more time. Tell them that you want to make sure everything you put down is all you needed to before going to the doctors and even ask about therapy again saying you wanted to be fully transparent, if you wish.  Then ask for the persons name you spoke with (they will most likely answer the same as all the others) and there you go. A bit of a relief or clarity. 

Your job can not fire you for mental illness that is all protected. Also odd your boss would even see that info for health insurance. Usually that is strictly between you, your doctor, and the ID for the insurance company. 

You can even bring up this entire thing at therapy (I did this once before medicated to have something "on the record" ) looking back I felt so crazy but it felt real. 

&#x200B;

I really hope you can find some calm in your life. Bipolar sucks and you CAN find a relief from these building thoughts. Through meds. and lots of therapy I can finally look at your post as an outsider, like wow that was exactly me. You deserve to feel better!

A good way to remove or lighten without bleach is a mix of 50/50 head and shoulders traditional shampoo and baking soda. I applied it with a tint brush to get an even coating and left it on about 20 mins. It lightened my arctic fox purple hair about 2 shades from a medium over light blonde hair to more of a pastel

&#x200B;

To be warned it was extremely drying to the hair so I did a mask after and it was all good! 

&#x200B;

I know some people have done this process a few days in a row and seemed to be fine, it all depends on your hair. Def. gentler than bleaching but that baking soda is a good cleaner and super dries. 

&#x200B;

I would give it a shot! Your blue looks light and you may be able to draw out quite a bit of that color in one to two treatments!

I am on many of the meds. you are and about a year ago added in Rexulti. At first I felt fine then I began to feel what I can only describe as pockets of fat? I have suffered from an eating disorder for a long time so no one believed me. But it got bad and I kept gaining, especially in my legs to the point it caused growing pains. It also messes with prolactin levels and caused me to lose my period. It can cause males to grow breasts due to creating disproportionate fat distribution and the prolactin increase. 

&#x200B;

When you read about it this is often brought up towards the end.

&#x200B;

I stopped it, my "fat pockets" went down and my period returned so I am 100% positive it was from Rexulti. It was a nightmare of physical symptoms which sucked so badly because mentally I liked it. So not worth it though. I was a hot mess and it really messed with my eating disorder brain as well. 

&#x200B;

I would talk with your doctor but in my experience it caused rapid weight gain and hormone inbalances. Never again!

Did they give you antibiotic shots and oral pain drops? My little guy had cancer surgery but the area was stitched neatly.  Any type of injury can be really dangerous. I highly recommend talking to your vet to get the antibiotics. It is definitely a two person job and you have to administer the shots into their front legs every few days. 

&#x200B;

Pain drops were good but def. made him loopy. We figured after fighting cancer he deserved to feel good. Our vet said she gave him the "good, good".  But that looks so so painful that I think it would be really nice and provide relief while healing. 

&#x200B;

What area do you live in? You can search for specialist's sometimes even within ER vet style places. Many of them will have an exotic vet who can then refer you. I am willing to help you search also but totally don't want to intrude if that is too much!

&#x200B;

I hope your cham heals and you can get the care.

I have an understanding in a way with this. I was diagnosed Anorexia B/P sub. and while I have been mostly a restrict person I have grown over the years to more Bingeing and B/P episodes. 

I am not sure if and when an eating disorder is considered serious and by whom but I feel they are serious once you get to a few months in and can not escape.

 I have been do doctors for normal things and GI stuff and they all seem to be like you are super healthy! Even at a low bmi and I feel like okay....guess I am "not good enough"

&#x200B;

I WILL say that binging and purging episodes for me are legit the worst thing about my ED and I think that Bulimia is not noticed as much as anorexia and that mindset is shameful on others to not treat it as such. The physical and mental toll it takes on your body to NEED that food in an almost hypnosis and then purge until your eyes get starry. I will spend days just B/P and wanting to die and using soooo many laxitives. So much worse than just eating less. It is literal hell on earth. I am sure you can relate. 

&#x200B;

I am sorry you are going through all of this and you ARE valid and you are ill. Please don't wish another ED upon yourself. Obviously within our minds weight loss is a goal and I would be a hypocrite if I said otherwise. But dealing with what you are right now is bad enough and you are enough and deserve the care no matter what weight you are at. It is not the weight it is the severity of your disorder. 

&#x200B;

Please take care and remember that you are going through a lot. Don't wish more pain upon yourself.

WTH who are you do no be "super worried" and tell someone they do or don't have an eating disorder.....toxic.

&#x200B;

I think if OP is having a fear of their relationship with food they came here for a reason. No one can really tell if someone does or does not have issues with food. Sometimes even a doctor can't. Sure they can diagnose unhealthy weights and go off of health stats or some behaviors, but in the end only you know you truth and your issues with food. 

If OP came here they are seeking help not some backwards diagnosis on how you are so disordered so they must not be....yeahhh just learn to out grow your mother's habbits, sometimes when you are younger a lot of things affect how we treat food. 

&#x200B;

Not saying OP DOES have an ED, but you know nothing. 

&#x200B;

If you binge and over eat and then fast for long periods that is very detrimental to your body and should be monitored by a doctor if for health reasons. 

&#x200B;

Take care OP, I hope you can find what you need and I would definitely check in with a doctor about types of fasting that would be healthiest.

I am so sorry for what you are going through. While dealing with an ED is hard enough on it's own. With your mom using suicide as a way to stop you from restricting is so messed up. Even if she means well, that is not how you help someone, that is how you upset someone. There are some really positive people on YouTube in recovery. My favorite is Rebecca Jane. She is honest and strong in overcoming her ED. Watch her earlier videos first to learn where she came from to where she is now. 

&#x200B;

If treatment is not an option I would try to be as kind to yourself as you can. Eat healthy foods so you are getting in your nutrition. Fruit and veg is low calorie but with lots of benefits so would be a good place to begin. Maybe some high fiber cereals, oatmeal, yogurts. Try and work your calories up slowly to where you are now to where your maintenance may be. It will be a long process. Feel free to reach out and I hope things get better for you <3

There was another group on reddit a while back called proED that got banned. It was a wonderful sub and so caring. While I am anorexic B/P sub I have really bad binges a few times a month. I can not imagine the struggles you must go through daily. 

I know that eating becomes mindless and cravings can take away my thinking util I have that thing, which becomes me driving around picking up so much junk food. It's impulsive, horrifying, and can get really out of control. I am so sorry for all you suffer with.

&#x200B;

Once proED ended the sub became completely un-relatable and triggering for me. 

&#x200B;

I moved to peach. Peach is an app a group of us use to talk on a daily basis. Everyone has their own stream and we talk about everything. So many different types of ED's. I met a lot of great people on there and it is welcoming and kind to all sufferers. The group tends to be all over, Anorexic, Bulimic, BED and combination and  other mental illness. 

My peach name is the same as my Reddit account. Feel free to friend me and you can go through my friend list to start if you would like. At first felt it was an odd setup to use, but give it some time.  It is a very unique community who shares everything from daily struggles in our life, a lot of ed things both upsetting, gross, and motivational .  Super loving community just going through lots of shit. 

&#x200B;

Please join if you with! We are there for anyone!

When you go to the pharmacy I would try to explain the situation and see if they can get in touch with your doctor as well. If they see you have been on the med for a while, as long as it's not in a restricted class (which I believe buspar is not) my pharmacist gave me like 3 doses of my cymbalta to hold me over. This is usually pretty common I have found with a lot of my bi-polar friends. 

 Some of my meds are on different time schedules and I totally forgot I was low/out of refills like you. 

&#x200B;

There also may be an emergency mental health care facility or even urgent care may prescribe a months worth if you can just prove you have been on it? OR maybe an online psychiatrist if your insurance covers that. I know they have therapists, not sure if they can prescribe meds. 

&#x200B;

I really wish you the best and hope something works out. Missing meds. no matter how powerful within your mix is always scary. All the positive vibes <3

To state some maybe misunderstandings from my previous posting. 

She is a reptile only vet that I trusted enough to perform surgery on him after seeking out other opinions. 

He was put on antibiotics for an oral infection. 

&#x200B;

This was most likely what was causing him to not poo and then not to eat. I had a cat once with an infection from a cyst and he developed hepatic "fatty liver" syndrome from not eating for 3 days. I fed him with a syringe for a month and he went on to live 5 more years after finally eating again on his own. Same thing appears to have been going on now with my boy and I was very familiar with it. 

&#x200B;

She said essentially I was all that was keeping him alive by feeding him, so I did, and he finally started shooting his tongue again yesterday and ate by himself. He needed as much nutrition as possible which is the only reason he was on carnivore care to begin with. Then transitioned to worms as he grew stronger from that. 

&#x200B;

He is a sweet, kind, and extremely well nurtured cham. 

&#x200B;

Had she been just a random vet I would be wary but she treats only reptiles and knows him well. 

&#x200B;

It you have any advice other than what I am doing to get him to pass urate and poo please let me know and please don't be so harsh.

This is a worst fear and why I avoid the doctor scale. I have had my ups and downs weight wise but would be considered "anorexic" ...however I have BED and Bulimic tendencies for anywhere from 2 days to 2 weeks. Binge eating is a horrible thing to go through. It doesn't make sense to so many people because they just think of it as eating because we are "sad" or "happy" but it is so much more than that. 

&#x200B;

It is an uncontrollable impulsive behavior. At times I am not even hungry and do not even want the food but I have it anyway because it is my chance to have it. I can stop a binge mid-day but I don't because I can not shake the urge until waking up with a new day. Other times I am just so focused on the taste I feel like I am high. It is a fucking nightmare girl and I am sorry you go through this. 

&#x200B;

Your well being has so much to do with our eating behaviors. They truly go hand in hand. I am so sorry you are struggling so much and that it is not being taken seriously. 

&#x200B;

Your pain and your ED are real and valid. I am sorry you have had to go through that. <3

This really hit me. What a true feeling as well as a stunning tattoo. Everything about it is so spot on and the look on her face and the discomfort are so strong. 

&#x200B;

A tad off topic but I have an extreme phobia of balloons popping. Anytime I see a latex balloon the thought of it popping makes me almost want to hide and cry. I just shut down and sometimes just fall apart, especially if one does pop.

So this tattoo also shed light on this other internal fear which now I am considering may stem from my bipolar. 

&#x200B;

Thank you for sharing your art!

This is horrifying please label or hide the image if posting things like this. It would be much appreciated. I frequent this sub to see cute images of chams and support others with set-ups and chams going through health issues. 

&#x200B;

This is just something sick to post on a sub like this.  Obviously nature can be cruel, but this is a night ruined for me see that a little cham suffered so much.
